540: #
541: #  `xlatch decl' above pre-fires exactly ONE colliding bit, #498's 1 << 6.  The
542: #  enum's OTHER already-used bits are #499's 1 << 7 (UNMAP_WR) and 1 << 8
543: #  (UNMAP_RD), and NO row in this file raises either before drawing -- so
544: #  aliasing SGIRE_W_PRIM_OP onto 1 << 7 or 1 << 8 left all 30 rows green while
545: #  making the decline go silent after ordinary unmapped traffic.  A one-token
546: #  edit to the very constant this round ADDED: floor clause (d), not coverage
547: #  debt.
548: #
549: #  The four handlers share one `d->warned', so the unmapped windows on sgi_re
550: #  set latches that the sgi_de draw path then tests.  Raising BOTH in one
551: #  session closes the remaining pair; with 1 << 6 above, every already-used bit
552: #  in the enum is now pre-set by some row.
